# {{ project_name }}

Kirby CMS site for [{{ domain }}](https://{{ domain }}), created from
[kirby-template-slothie-studio](https://github.com/slothiestudio/kirby-template-slothie-studio).

## Setup

```bash
composer install
npm install
```

Needs PHP {{ php_version }}+ and Node 24.

## Development

```bash
npm run dev
```

Runs PHP's built-in server on `localhost:8888`{% if frontend == 'vite' %} together with the Vite dev server{% endif %}.
Create the first Panel account at `/panel` (Kirby only allows that on localhost).
{%- if frontend == 'vite' %}

```bash
npm run build     # build src/ into public_html/dist
npm run preview   # build and serve
```
{%- endif %}

## Format

```bash
npm run format        # apply
npm run format:check  # check (runs in CI)
```

Prettier, Stylelint and ECS (PHP, PSR-12 with 2-space indentation).

## Languages

{{ default_lang }} is the default language at `/`{% for code in langs[1:] %}, {{ code }} lives under `/{{ code }}`{% endfor %}.
Languages are configured in `site/languages/`; content files carry the language code
(`home.{{ default_lang }}.txt`). UI texts (404 page, skip link) are translated in the language files.

## Deployment

- `main` deploys to https://{{ preview_domain }}
- `live` deploys to https://{{ domain }}

The workflows in `.github/workflows/` call the shared ones in
[slothiestudio/kirby-workflows](https://github.com/slothiestudio/kirby-workflows). Every push to
`main` keeps a "Release: main → live" PR up to date; merging it (with a merge commit) releases to live.

Setup on GitHub:

- Environments `preview` and `Live` with secrets `SERVER_URL`, `USERNAME`, `SSH_KEY` or `PASSWORD`
  (optional `SSH_PASSPHRASE`, `SSH_FINGERPRINT`) and the variable `SERVER_DIRECTORY` (the project root)
- Settings → Actions → General: allow GitHub Actions to create pull requests

On the servers: PHP {{ php_version }}+, document root `public_html/`.
{%- if seo %} Kirby SEO 2 needs a license per live domain: activate it in the Panel under "Metadata & SEO".{% endif %}
{%- if staticache %}

Pages are cached as static HTML in `public_html/static/` (Staticache) and served by Apache without PHP.
Kirby clears the cache on content changes and every deploy deletes it. Caching is off on localhost.
{%- endif %}

## Template updates

```bash
copier update   # pulls changes from kirby-template-slothie-studio as a diff
```

Your answers are stored in `.copier-answers.yml`. Starter files the site owns (content, templates,
blueprints, header/footer, CSS/JS, this README) are never overwritten.

## Folder structure

```
content/        → Kirby content{% if not content_in_git %} (gitignored, lives on the server){% endif %}
public_html/    → web root (index.php, .htaccess{% if frontend == 'vite' %}, dist/ = built assets{% else %}, assets/{% endif %}{% if staticache %}, static/ = page cache{% endif %})
site/
  blueprints/
  config/       → config.php + per-domain overrides
  languages/
  plugins/      → installed by Composer (gitignored)
  snippets/     → layout, head, header, footer, language switcher
  templates/
{%- if frontend == 'vite' %}
src/            → CSS (Tailwind) and JS, built by Vite
{%- endif %}
storage/        → accounts, cache, sessions (gitignored)
```
